     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, or 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. This order is about twice that. A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 850 mg to 1,000 mg per dose. A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg** three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day), the usual maximum\n- **500 mg** three times daily with meals (1,500 mg/day)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is what you want, tell me and add a clinical rationale. I can then enter it with a note, though I'd suggest a pharmacist review it first. If you give me the corrected dose, I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
